DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppbbmmttooaasscciiii  reads  a  PBM  image as input and produces a somewhat crude
       ASCII graphic image as output.

       To convert back, use aasscciiiittooppggmm(1).

       ppppmmttootteerrmm does a similar thing for color  images  to  be  displayed  on
       color text terminals.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppbbmmttooaasscciiii recognizes the
       following command line options:

       The --11xx22 and --22xx44 options give you two alternate ways for the pixels to
       get mapped to characters.  With 11xx22, the default, each character repre‐
       sents  a  group  of  1  pixel across by 2 pixels down.  With --22xx44, each
       character represents 2 pixels across by 4 pixels down.   With  the  1x2
       mode  you  can see the individual pixels, so it's useful for previewing
       small images on a non-graphics terminal.  The 2x4 mode lets you display
       larger  images on a small display, but it obscures pixel-level details.
       2x4 mode is also good for displaying PGM images:

       pamscale -width 158 | pnmnorm | pamditherbw -threshold | pbmtoascii -2x4


       should give good results.


